        "original_id": "187a6e0a-b887-5461-970f-134fcebc052d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vincenzo Bellini, Mikhail Glinka\n- Works: I puritani\n- Topics: Opera, classical music\n\nFacts:\n- Vincenzo Bellini was born on 3 November 1801 and died on 23 September 1835.\n- Mikhail Glinka was born on 1 June 1804 (20 May O.S.) and died on 15 February 1857 (3 February O.S.).\n- Vincenzo Bellini was an Italian opera composer known for his long-flowing melodic lines and was called \"the Swan of Catania.\"\n- Mikhail Glinka was the first Russian composer to gain wide recognition within Russia and is often regarded as the fountainhead of Russian classical music.\n- I puritani (\"The Puritans\") is an opera by Vincenzo Bellini.",
